  "what_it_means": "Both series re-normalised over the half hours they share, so this is a difference in the physics and not in the coverage. `spread_overstated_by` compares max/min on both sides -- the whole range, two half hours wide. `p95_spread_overstated_by` compares the dirtiest-5%-over-cleanest-5% spread on both sides, which is the statistic the customer page prints and therefore the only one a sentence about that page's figure may use. Neither is a correction to apply to a HOUSEHOLD: how wrong this shape is for one home depends on when that home drew, and that is measured per household in the paired `published` value on each record."
 },
